<Base
  title="Board positions"
  description="Who can stand for the E.R.I.C. board, and when the election happens."
>
  <main id="content" class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="kicker">Board</p>
      <h1>Stand for the next board</h1>
      <p>The round that closed on Tuesday 31 March at 23:59 CET has ended. The path below is the one the bylaws describe for the following year.</p>
    </header>
    <h2>Who can stand</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A Rotaractor from an E.R.I.C. member district, at least 18, and fluent in English.</li>
      <li>Someone who has already served as a country representative, a board member, a board assistant, or a district Rotaract representative.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How the election works</h2>
    <div class="year">
      <strong>1</strong>
      <p>Send the application, a Rotaract CV, and a motivation letter to board@rotaracteurope.eu. President: up to four weeks before the winter REM. Other offices: up to four weeks before EUCO.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="year">
      <strong>2</strong>
      <p>The president and secretary check that each candidacy is valid, three weeks before EUCO.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="year">
      <strong>3</strong>
      <p>The president is elected at the winter REM. The other offices are elected at EUCO.</p>
    </div>
    <h2>The offices</h2>
    <p>President, vice-president, secretary, treasurer, marketing and communication, social service, and information technology. The president and vice-president cannot hold a second board office at the same time. Role descriptions sit in the bylaws, which are still published on the current site under Resources.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
